WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.468
-Today is Friday, and that's
usually when I catch up

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.502
with some of my personal stuff.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:04.737
I check my inbox,
I return my emails,

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.672
and, of course,
I send out "thank you" notes.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.307
And I was just running --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:09.742
I'm so busy with the holidays,

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:10.976
I thought
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:12.078
I would like to write out

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.079
my weekly "thank you" notes
right now.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.147
Is that all right?

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.015
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.149
James,
can I get some

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:18.684
"thank you" note writing music,
please?

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:19.819 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.187
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.589
He's always in a good mood,
that guy.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.589
-Yeah.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:26.326 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.529 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.898 line:0%
-Thank you,
the omicron variant,

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:34.501 line:0%
for sounding like
a paperback thriller

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.502 line:0%
you'd buy at an airport
Hudson News.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.905
[ Applause ]
Omicron variant.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.976
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.082 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:54.186 line:0%
Thank you, new "Magic Mike"
sequel and online shopping,

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:56.755 line:0%
for both guaranteeing
the delivery of many packages.

00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:59.225
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:01.795
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.430 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.567
-Thank you, decorating
the house with Christmas lights.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.369
It's cold, icy and slippery --

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.471
perfect time for Dad
to get up on the roof.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.339
[ Applause ]

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.207
-Just get up there!
Come on!

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:17.010
-[ High-pitched ]
Don't ruin Christmas, Dad!

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.612
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.914 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.982
Thank you, holiday shopping,

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.051
for being that special time
of year where you think,

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.253
"This friendship
may be worth $35,

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.789
but it's not worth $7 more
for shipping."

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.924
[ Applause ]

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.092
Come on.
-Come on!

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.860
-That's --

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.995
-New Year's present.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.430
-Yeah.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.664 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:40.699
Thank you, gift receipts,

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:42.735
for always keeping the price
a secret --

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.671
well, right until
they return it.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.005
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.274
[ Applause ]

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.678 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.215
Thank you,
Christmas tree stands,

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.716
for letting me kick off
the holidays

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.319
by putting my tree
in a medieval torture device.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.154
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.055
[ Applause ]

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:04.224
-It's leaning!

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.726
[ Jimmy and Steve chuckle ]

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:07.960 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.264
-Thank you, sidewalk salt,
for being margarita salt

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.232
that quit partying
and got a job.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.534
There you go.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.301
Those are my "thank you" notes
right there.

00:02:16.301 --> 00:02:17.403
Thank you, everybody!

